From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GE-Proton <git@localhost>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winebus: Optionally expose DualShock 4 v2 as v1

Add PROTON_SONY_DUALSHOCK4_V2_AS_V1=1 to expose a native
second-generation DualShock 4 (054c:09cc) directly as a first-generation
model (054c:05c4).

When PROTON_SONY_DUALSENSE_AS_DUALSHOCK4 is also enabled, resolve the
DualSense or DualSense Edge target directly to DS4 v1. Keep the existing
DualSense-to-DS4 report translator, but expose the genuine DS4 v1 report
descriptor and firmware identity instead of first presenting a v2 device.

Native DS4 v2 input and output reports share the v1 common wire layout.
Translate the Bluetooth transport wrappers and calibration report where
needed while retaining the physical identity internally for audio,
haptics, containers, and hotplug handling.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_udev.c b/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_udev.c
index 2e7729fd..c516d803 100644
--- a/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_udev.c
+++ b/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_udev.c
@@ -1519,6 +1519,13 @@ static BOOL spoof_dualsense_as_dualshock4(void)
     return env && env[0] == '1' && !env[1];
 }
 
+static BOOL spoof_dualshock4_v2_as_v1(void)
+{
+    const char *env = getenv("PROTON_SONY_DUALSHOCK4_V2_AS_V1");
+
+    return env && env[0] == '1' && !env[1];
+}
+
